error[T0820] classes.tov:65:3: instances of `ListNode` can reference each other in a cycle, which reference counting alone can't free
   65 |   next: ListNode | undefined = undefined
  cycle: ListNode.next → ListNode
  fix: cycles are real: declare `cyclic class ListNode`: its instances are also checked by the cycle collector
  fix: a back-reference: mark it `weak next` (a parent pointer, say): it then doesn't keep its target alive
  fix: set once: make it `readonly next` and set it in the constructor: objects then only point to older objects
  fix[maybe]: declare `cyclic class ListNode`

error[T0815] classes.tov:75:8: a `weak` field must have type `C | undefined` for a class `C`, found `int`
   75 |   weak bad: int = 0
  why: a weak reference doesn't keep its target alive, so it reads as `undefined` once the target is freed

